<node id="Femme">
  <data key="d0">Femme</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Femme refers to various female individuals, representing a diverse group with differing ages, professions, and perspectives on quality of life. The descriptions highlight the experiences and beliefs of these women, demonstrating their roles in both professional and personal contexts.

Among the individuals, there are notable representations of those aged 20, 47, 54, 63, 69, and 70. For instance, a 20-year-old female is identified mainly as a student, implying her current educational pursuits. A 54-year-old civil servant is described multiple times, focusing on her advocacy for access to culture through institutions like museums and theaters, her dedication to managing work-life balance, and her commitment to environmental issues such as water management and waste sorting.

Additionally, a 63-year-old civil servant emphasizes the significance of proximity services and available health services as essential elements for enhancing quality of life. This individual points out that removal of transportation barriers contributes greatly to convenience and well-being. From the group of women aged 47, there are two individuals in managerial roles, both stressing the importance of access to education and essential services to maintain a reasonable standard of living and well-being.

The description also includes a retired woman aged 70, who holds strong views on environmental preservation, recognizing the importance of air and water quality and the need for rich biodiversity. This retired individual also values social relationships, viewing them as crucial for preventing isolation and fostering meaningful exchanges. Another 70-year-old woman from the same cohort believes that cultural access is vital for personal emancipation, reinforcing its importance in promoting individual well-being.

Lastly, a 69-year-old female in a different profession highlights not only the value of cultural access but also the significance of family and community relationships, advocating for a balance between public responsibilities and private life. This diversity of ages and experiences encapsulates a broader narrative of how different facets of life impact women's roles and well-being across various societal aspects.&lt;SEP&gt;A gender category referring to the female sex, represented by individuals who identify as women.&lt;SEP&gt;A female individual with various age, profession, and quality of life dimensions throughout the input text.&lt;SEP&gt;A female individual mentioned across multiple verbatims with varying attributes including age and profession.&lt;SEP&gt;A human individual identifying as female.&lt;SEP&gt;A female individual referenced in the verbatims with an age of 37, who is employed and provides insights on quality of life dimensions including environment and culture.&lt;SEP&gt;Women are noted as the majority among survey respondents, influencing the prioritization of topics such as health and the environment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-bc2a4c9fbcd8f37dfe48f336cbbe23d7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bc2a4c9fbcd8f37dfe48f336cbbe23d7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bc2a4c9fbcd8f37dfe48f336cbbe23d7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c6e43bd634411734a6b905f38e6c188f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2cde183c2f8365b319d177367a294261-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2cde183c2f8365b319d177367a294261-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2cde183c2f8365b319d177367a294261-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9d0d1641d86faa1a8df6dd5a1e615c1d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-37b4833e5a4ced914cfa6572c9de7980-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1787573503</data>
